\id EZR - Berean Standard Bible
\h Ezra
\toc2 Ezra
\toc1 Ezra
\mt1 Ezra
\c 1
\s1 The Proclamation of Cyrus
\r (2 Chronicles 36:22–23; Isaiah 45:1–25)
\m
\v 1 \zdate|Q8423:P39:Q3114558:P580\*In the first year of \zwd Cyrus king of Persia|Q8423\zwd*, to fulfill the word of the LORD spoken through \zwd Jeremiah|id="Q158825" t="2"\zwd*, the LORD stirred the spirit of \zwd Cyrus king of Persia|Q8423\zwd* to send a proclamation throughout his kingdom and to put it in writing as follows:
\b
\pmo
\v 2 “This is what \zwd Cyrus king of Persia|Q8423\zwd* says:
\b
\pmo ‘The LORD, the God of heaven, who has given me all the kingdoms of the earth, has appointed me to build a house for Him at Jerusalem in Judah.
\b
\pmo
\v 3 Whoever among you belongs to His people, may his God be with him, and may he go to Jerusalem in Judah and build the house of the LORD, the God of Israel; He is the God who is in Jerusalem.
\v 4 And let every survivor, wherever he lives, be assisted by the men of that region with silver, gold, goods, and livestock, along with a freewill offering for the house of God in Jerusalem.’”
\b
\m
\v 5 So the family heads of Judah and Benjamin, along with the priests and Levites—everyone whose spirit God had stirred—prepared to go up and rebuild the house of the LORD in Jerusalem.
\b
\m
\v 6 And all their neighbors supported them with articles of silver and gold, with goods and livestock, and with valuables, in addition to all their freewill offerings.
\s1 Cyrus Restores the Holy Vessels
\b
\m
\v 7 \zwd King Cyrus|Q8423\zwd* also brought out the articles belonging to the house of the LORD that \zwd Nebuchadnezzar|id="Q12591" t="2"\zwd* had carried away from Jerusalem and placed in the temple of his gods.
\v 8 \zwd Cyrus king of Persia|Q8423\zwd* had them brought out by the hand of \zwd Mithredath the treasurer|Q55649336\zwd*, who counted them out to \zwd Sheshbazzar the prince of Judah|Q94258346\zwd*.\f + \fr 1:8 \ft That is, the leader of the exiles returning to Judah\f*
\v 9 This was the inventory:
\b
\li1 30 gold dishes,\f + \fr 1:9 \ft Or basins; twice in this verse\f*
\b
\li1 1,000 silver dishes,
\b
\li1 29 silver utensils,
\b
\li1
\v 10 30 gold bowls,
\b
\li1 410 matching silver bowls,
\b
\li1 and 1,000 other articles.
\b
\m
\v 11 In all, there were 5,400 gold and silver articles. \zwd Sheshbazzar|Q94258346\zwd* brought all these along when the exiles went up from Babylon to Jerusalem.
\c 2
\s1 The List of Returning Exiles
\r (Nehemiah 7:4–69)
\m 
\v 1 Now these are the people of the province who came up from the captivity of the exiles carried away to Babylon by \zwd Nebuchadnezzar|id="Q12591" t="2"\zwd* its king. They returned to Jerusalem and Judah, each to his own town, 
\v 2 accompanied by \zwd Zerubbabel|Q320139\zwd*, \zwd Jeshua|\zwd*, \zwd Nehemiah|\zwd*, \zwd Seraiah|\zwd*, \zwd Reelaiah|\zwd*, \zwd Mordecai|\zwd*, \zwd Bilshan|\zwd*, \zwd Mispar|Q6884731\zwd*, \zwd Bigvai|\zwd*, \zwd Rehum|\zwd*, and \zwd Baanah|Q139600850\zwd*.\f + \fr 2:2 \ft Parallel text at Nehemiah 7:7 accompanied by Zerubbabel, Jeshua, Nehemiah, Azariah, Raamiah, Nahamani, Mordecai, Bilshan, Mispereth, Bigvai, Nehum, and Baanah\f* 
\b
\m This is the count of the men of Israel: 
\b
\li1 
\v 3 the descendants of \zwd Parosh|id="Q1577528" t="2"\zwd*, 2,172; 
\b
\li1 
\v 4 the descendants of \zwd Shephatiah|\zwd*, 372; 
\b
\li1 
\v 5 the descendants of \zwd Arah|id="Q138782353" t="2"\zwd*, 775; 
\b
\li1 
\v 6 the descendants of \zwd Pahath-moab|id="Q7124538" t="2"\zwd* (through the line of \zwd Jeshua|\zwd* and \zwd Joab|\zwd*), 2,812; 
\b
\li1 
\v 7 the descendants of \zwd Elam|\zwd*, 1,254; 
\b
\li1 
\v 8 the descendants of \zwd Zattu|id="Q138862840" t="2"\zwd*, 945; 
\b
\li1 
\v 9 the descendants of \zwd Zaccai|id="Q139008708" t="2"\zwd*, 760; 
\b
\li1 
\v 10 the descendants of \zwd Bani|\zwd*,\f + \fr 2:10 \ft Bani is a variant of Binnui; see Nehemiah 7:15.\f* 642; 
\b
\li1 
